        <briefdescription>
<para>Homogenizes per-microplane normal and in-plane shear stresses to the macroscopic stress, in Voigt notation. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Approximates the continuum microplane virtual-work homogenization over the unit hemisphere:    <formula id="330">\[  \sigma_{ij} = \frac{3}{2\pi} \int_\Omega \left( \sigma_N N_{ij} + \sigma_L L_{ij} + \sigma_M M_{ij} \right)
\, d\Omega
\]</formula> by the quadrature sum actually evaluated here, in which the hemisphere-integral normalization constant is already absorbed into the integration weights <formula id="323">$ w^{(m)} $</formula> (see Discretization::get(), where <formula id="325">$ \sum_m w^{(m)} = 3 $</formula>):    <formula id="331">\[  \sigma_{ij} \approx \sum_{m=1}^{n_{qp}} w^{(m)} \left( \sigma_N^{(m)} N_{ij}^{(m)}
    + \sigma_M^{(m)} M_{ij}^{(m)} + \sigma_L^{(m)} L_{ij}^{(m)} \right)
\]</formula> <parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Scalar type of the per-microplane stresses, e.g. <computeroutput>double</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>autodiff::dual</computeroutput>; the projection tensors <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_continuum_mechanics_1_1_microplane_1_1_n_t_split_1a47ec82902b03ef84633f1b19ef9f19d0" kindref="member">pTensors</ref> stay <computeroutput>double</computeroutput> (they are geometric constants, never differentiated), so <computeroutput>T</computeroutput> may differ from <computeroutput>double</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
