    <briefdescription>
<para>Normal-tangential (N-T) split and projection tensors of the microplane theory, as used by the M7-family models (MicroplaneM7, GM7). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>On each microplane, the macroscopic strain is projected onto the normal direction <formula id="312">$ n^{(m)} $</formula> and the two in-plane orthogonal shear directions <formula id="313">$ l^{(m)} $</formula>, <formula id="314">$ m^{(m)} $</formula> (spanning the plane orthogonal to <formula id="312">$ n^{(m)} $</formula>), giving a normal strain <formula id="315">$ \varepsilon_N $</formula> and two shear strains <formula id="316">$ \varepsilon_M, \varepsilon_L $</formula>. <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_continuum_mechanics_1_1_microplane_1_1_n_t_split_1a47ec82902b03ef84633f1b19ef9f19d0" kindref="member">pTensors</ref> holds the corresponding Voigt-notation projection tensors <formula id="317">$ N_{ij} = n_i n_j $</formula>, <formula id="318">$ M_{ij} = \tfrac{1}{2}(m_i n_j + m_j n_i) $</formula>, <formula id="319">$ L_{ij} = \tfrac{1}{2}(l_i n_j + l_j n_i) $</formula>, built from the hard-coded discretization (Discretization::get()), and <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_continuum_mechanics_1_1_microplane_1_1_n_t_split_1ae32dc8189cbfce09adcf8dec27c140ef" kindref="member">homogenizeStress</ref> / <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_continuum_mechanics_1_1_microplane_1_1_n_t_split_1a8b54f86df9f3296595e3a0ccf1983508" kindref="member">homogenizeTangent</ref> perform the virtual-work homogenization of per-microplane normal/shear stresses and tangents back to the macroscopic stress and tangent. <parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>scheme</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The <ref refid="namespace_marmot_1_1_continuum_mechanics_1_1_microplane_1af92b719bb2e032a4645d5e37f808cbd1" kindref="member">QuadratureScheme</ref> (and thus the number of microplanes <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_continuum_mechanics_1_1_microplane_1_1_n_t_split_1ac4c4bf30b23d1e109496ecd4328b7340" kindref="member">nqp</ref>) this instantiation is built for. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
